/** * Java FFM (java.lang.foreign) binding for the MCDR native render library. * * <p>This class replaces `Dx12Native` from the Fabric original. Every method keeps * the name and signature of its JNI counterpart so the rest of the backend ports with a * class-name change only; what changed is the mechanism: * * <ul> *   <li>`System.load` + `javac -h` generated `Java_com_..._*` exports are *       gone. [SymbolLookup.libraryLookup] loads the DLL and resolves *       plain `extern "C"` symbols — the native side is a pure C-ABI library with no *       knowledge of Java.</li> *   <li>Structs cross the boundary through [dev.nts.expdxr.d3d12.extern.MCDRLayout] group layouts instead of the *       hand-written little-endian `putInt`/`putU8` packing that the JNI *       bridge needed. [MCDRLayout.verify] checks every offset against the running *       DLL at load time, so a drifted header is a startup error instead of silent memory *       corruption.</li> *   <li>Handles stay plain `long` addresses (the Java side never dereferences them), *       converted to [MemorySegment] only at the call boundary.</li> *   <li>Errors arrive through [D3D12LastError] instead of a thrown Java exception *       raised from native code, so a failure inside a hot call no longer unwinds through *       the JNI frame.</li> * </ul> * * <p>All method handles are linked once and invoked with `invokeExact`; nothing on a * per-frame path allocates a [MethodHandle]. */object MCDR_ABI {
    /**     * 高频诊断日志开关：由日志级别决定 —— 配置文件 `[logging] logLevel = DEBUG`（或更低），     * 环境变量 `DX12_LOG_VERBOSE=1` 仍是开发期逃生口。Java 端每帧/每调用的诊断打印均以此门控，     * 避免海量 System.err 同步 I/O 拖垮帧率（P29 帧数修复）。     */
    val LOG_VERBOSE: Boolean
        get() = IllusionLogger.debugEnabled()
    /**     * 帧时间插桩开关（P3）：配置 `[debug] profiling`，默认关闭。与 LOG_VERBOSE 分离——     * 后者会附带大量诊断日志，会干扰计时。     */
    val PROF: Boolean
        get() = D3D12Settings.profiling || LOG_VERBOSE
    private const val LIB_NAME = "MCDR.dll"
    private const val EXTRACT_DIR = "dxrmc"
    /**     * Third-party SDK runtimes that ride inside the mod JAR and are unpacked next to MCDR.dll.     *     * <p>The manifest is generated by the Gradle `stageVendorLibs` task at the moment the files     * are staged, so it can never disagree with what was actually packaged — a JAR directory     * cannot be enumerated, and hard-coding the names here would let the two lists drift.     *     * <p>Only **Intel XeSS** is packaged (`libxess.dll`, `libxess_fg.dll`, `libxell.dll` plus     * `LICENSE-xess.txt`): Intel's licence permits binary redistribution provided the notice     * travels with it. The Intel-only build is a release decision, not a licensing one — the     * AMD FidelityFX runtimes are redistributable too, but a shipped build no longer carries     * them (2026-10-20), so FSR simply reports itself unavailable there. The NVIDIA runtime     * DLLs may not be redistributed at all — their licence forbids use that would place the SDK     * under an open-source licence, which is what packaging it in an LGPL-2.1 mod would do.     * Dev builds put both AMD and NVIDIA runtimes in `run/dxrmc/` (`gradlew copyVendorDlls`,     * wired as a `runClient` dependency).     */
