    /**     * P97: set the variable-rate-shading granularity (D3D12 `RSSetShadingRate`).     *     * <p>The value is only recorded in the native device context; the native layer re-issues the     * call on every graphics command list it starts (`ID3D12CommandList::Reset` clears list state),     * which is what makes this setting work without a game restart.     *     * @param rate raw `D3D12_SHADING_RATE` (1X1=0x0 1X2=0x1 2X1=0x4 2X2=0x5 2X4=0x6 4X2=0x9     *     4X4=0xA), or -1 for "issue no call at all" (the device keeps its default 1x1).     * @return 1 when accepted - including the normal case where the request arrives before the     *     device exists and is therefore gated later, on the first command list - 0 when this     *     device cannot honour the rate (VRS tier 0, or `2X4`/`4X2`/`4X4` without     *     `AdditionalShadingRatesSupported`; only answerable once the device exists), -1 for a rate     *     the native layer does not know, and [Int.MIN_VALUE] when the loaded native DLL predates     *     this export. Never throws: this is a diagnostic path.     */
